      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I like this idea.\nI also think that avatars marked NSFW should by default be greyed out if you're in a public world (just a client side check).\nThe NSFW tags could be used to prevent most accidents (sometimes switching avatars too fast causes it to not change for some players, etc.)\n\nBut VRChat might not be able to add this feature as they need the game to have the 13+ rating. Adding a \"hide mature avatars\" setting is basically the same as allowing mature avatars to be uploaded in the first place.\n\nThey'd at least need some excuse like \"we're adding the system so people can tag their spooky halloween avatars\"",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
